Q: Making base color utility class in Tailwind A: <p>There's currently no native way to do this. Your request is reasonable, and it has been raised with the Tailwind CSS team before, but it does not seem to be a priority at the moment.</p>
<p>You can solve it with a JavaScript plugin.</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="false" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const shades = [
  '50',
  '100',
  '200',
  '300',
  '400',
  '500',
  '600',
  '700',
  '800',
  '900',
  '950',
]

tailwind.config = {
  theme: {
    extend: {
      colors: {
        base: tailwind.colors.sky,
      },
    },
  },
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;div class="size-32 bg-base-500"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
<p>Of course, the code example is written for v3, where you can implement ad hoc JavaScript plugins directly via the CDN.</p>
<p>In v4, you need to create a JavaScript file and add it using the <code>@plugin</code> directive:</p>
<p><strong>myplugin.mjs</strong></p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>import plugin from 'tailwindcss/plugin'

const baseColor = 'sky'

const shades = [
  '50',
  '100',
  '200',
  '300',
  '400',
  '500',
  '600',
  '700',
  '800',
  '900',
  '950',
]

export default plugin(
  function () {},
  {
    theme: {
      extend: {
        colors: {
          base: Object.fromEntries(
            shades.map((shade) =&gt; [
              shade,
              `var(--color-${baseColor}-${shade})`,
            ]),
          ),
        },
      },
    },
  },
)
</code></pre>
<p><strong>app.css</strong></p>
<pre class="lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>@import &quot;tailwindcss&quot;;

@plugin &quot;./myplugin.mjs&quot;;
</code></pre>
<p>Of course, a <code>base-*</code> utility could also be implemented with a JavaScript plugin. The goal is not entirely clear here, so I only tried to share the simplest way to copy/alias the color scale.</p>

Q: Spring Boot get spring.profiles.active value in a static block A: <p>Please use below tool in static to obtain env variable</p>
<pre><code>import org.springframework.beans.BeansException;
import org.springframework.context.ApplicationContext;
import org.springframework.context.ApplicationContextAware;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Lazy;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;
import org.springframework.beans.factory.DisposableBean;

@Service
@Lazy(false)
public class SpringContextHolder implements ApplicationContextAware, DisposableBean{
    private static ApplicationContext applicationContext = null;

    public static ApplicationContext getApplicationContext() {
        return applicationContext;
    }

    public static void clearHolder() {
        applicationContext = null;
    }

    @Override
    public void destroy() throws Exception {
        SpringContextHolder.clearHolder();
    }

    @Override
    public void setApplicationContext(ApplicationContext applicationContext) throws BeansException {
        SpringContextHolder.applicationContext = applicationContext;
    }
}

</code></pre>
<p>how to use</p>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>import org.springframework.core.env.Environment;

//--- pass some code
@SpringBootApplication
public class MyApplication {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SpringApplication.run(MyApplication.class, args);

        Environment environment = SpringContextHolder.getApplicationContext().getEnvironment();
        System.out.println(environment.getProperty(&quot;spring.profiles.active&quot;));
    }

}


</code></pre>

Q: How do I use vuelidate with an array of objects? A: <p>It should be noted in Vuelidate 3 the $each helper param suggested in the other answer <strong>has been removed</strong>.</p>
<p><a href="https://vuelidate-next.netlify.app/migration_guide.html#removal-of-each-param" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://vuelidate-next.netlify.app/migration_guide.html#removal-of-each-param</a></p>
<p>Instead, you are expected to create a nested Vue component which handles each object in the array, and make use of nested validations.</p>
<p>This is the example given in the link above, in case this page is removed from their documentation in the future.</p>
<p>Wrapper Component:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;!-- PeopleList.vue --&gt;
&lt;template&gt;
  &lt;div&gt;
    &lt;PersonInput
      v-for=&quot;(person, index) of people&quot;
      :person=&quot;person&quot;
      :key=&quot;index&quot;
      @updatePerson=&quot;person = $event&quot;
    /&gt;
    &lt;!-- This list will include all errors,
         both from this component and errors from every &lt;PersonInput&gt; --&gt;
    &lt;div v-for=&quot;error of v$.$errors&quot; :key=&quot;error.$uid&quot;&gt;
      {{ error.$message }}
    &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/template&gt;

&lt;script&gt;
import { useVuelidate } from '@vuelidate/core'
import PersonInput from '@/components/PersonInput'

export default {
  components: { PersonInput },
  setup () {
    return { v$: useVuelidate() }
  },
  data() {
    return {
      people: [ { name: 'John' }, { name: '' } ]
    }
  },
  validations: {
    people: {
      required,
      minLength: minLength(3),
    }
  }
}
&lt;/script&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Nested component:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;!-- PersonInput.vue --&gt;
&lt;template&gt;
  &lt;div&gt;
    &lt;input type=&quot;text&quot; :value=&quot;person.name&quot; @input=&quot;$emit('updatePerson', { name: $event })&quot; /&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/template&gt;

&lt;script&gt;
import { useVuelidate } from '@vuelidate/core'

export default {
  props: {
    person: { type: Object, required: true },
  },
  setup () {
    return { v$: useVuelidate() }
  },
  validations: {
    person: {
      required,
      minLength: minLength(2),
    }
  }
}
&lt;/script&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: How to safely use $_SERVER[&#39;REMOTE_ADDR&#39;] and $_SERVER[&#39;HTTP_USER_AGENT&#39;] A: <p>First of all there must be sanity.</p>
<pre><code>$ip = isset( sanitize_text_field( wp_unslash( $_SERVER['REMOTE_ADDR'] )));
</code></pre>
<p>Or run a complete screen</p>
<pre><code>$ip = isset( $_SERVER['REMOTE_ADDR'] ) ? $_SERVER['REMOTE_ADDR'] : '';
$sanitized_ip = filter_var( $ip, FILTER_VALIDATE_IP );

if ( false === $sanitized_ip ) {
    // The value was not a valid IP address
    $sanitized_ip = '0.0.0.0';
}
</code></pre>
<p>But at the least, you must check for an <code>issett()</code> or <code>is_empty()</code> to check the index exists before using it (<code>WordPress.Security.ValidatedSanitizedInput.InputNotValidated</code>)</p>
